-- Q_GWT
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='$\mathrm{Q}_{\mathrm{GWT}}$ & l/d & Greywater treatment capacity | In addition to the greywater and service water qualities, the decisive dimensioning factor for a greywater reuse system is the necessary daily treatment capacity. The daily service water demand and greywater inflow should be compared with each other. Decisive for the hydraulic dimensioning is the smaller value in each case. | The treatment capacity can be determined as follows: | Q_{\mathrm{GWT}}=Q_{\mathrm{GW}} \text {, when } Q_{\mathrm{SW}}>Q_{\mathrm{GW}}(\mathrm{l} / \mathrm{d})  \tag{3} | Q_{\mathrm{GWT}}=Q_{\mathrm{SW}} \text {, when } Q_{\mathrm{GW}}>Q_{\mathrm{SW}}(\mathrm{l} / \mathrm{d}) \tag{4} — printed p.10 / p.27–28', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.2 Symbols; §9.4 Eq.(3)/(4), printed p.10 / p.27–28 derived) [VC] — derived — Eq.(3)/(4) output', verified_at=now() where id='1f5bb38f-8cb7-45f3-a116-01656eb08a82' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
