-- Q_SW_P
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='$\mathrm{Q}_{\text {SW-P }}$ & l/d & Person-specific service water demand | Besides the service water quantity, the quality requirements for service water should be also defined by the planner according to the classifications described in Section 6.2. The following Table 5 provides assistance in determining the service water demand. | Table 5: Daily water consumption in household according to application (Source: BDEW 2015) | Consumer & Household consumption in litres per capita and day | Toilets & 33 | Personal hygiene & 44 | Washing machine & 15 | Cleaning/Irrigation & 7 | Cooking/Drinking & 5 | Kitchen/Dishwasher & 7 — printed p.10 / p.25', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.2 Symbols; §9.2 Table 5, printed p.10 / p.25 derived) [VC] — duplicate of ws 05; Table 5 values are BDEW 2015 household averages offered as "assistance", not limits; the List of Tables prints Table 5 at p.24, the table sits in §9.2 (p.25)', verified_at=now() where id='894c951f-f35f-4634-8a10-0495e5eab748' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- Q_SW_A
